        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Agent: Prototypically, agents are flesh-and-blood sources of an action, but for our purposes, an agent is the seeming source of any action, an entity without which the action could not occur: She criticized the program in this report. Often, we can make the means by which we do something a seeming agent: This report criticizes the program. Do not confuse agents with subjects. Agents prototypically are subjects, but an agent can be in a grammatical object: I was arrested and interrogated by the police.",
